Modifications
-------------

As required by section 4(b) of the Apache License, the following files carry
modifications relative to upstream Pingora 0.9.0:

  pingora-core/src/listeners/tls/rustls/mod.rs
      Adds `TlsSettings::with_server_config`, which accepts a caller-built
      `rustls::ServerConfig`. Upstream `TlsSettings::build()` constructs its own
      configuration with a fixed protocol-version and cipher-suite profile, so
      a caller cannot narrow either, nor control session storage or ticketing.
      (Upstream 0.9.0 added `set_cert_resolver`, `set_client_cert_verifier`
      and `Acceptor::from_server_config`; none of them yields a `TlsSettings`
      built from a complete `ServerConfig`, which is what a listener takes.)

  pingora-proxy/src/proxy_trait.rs
  pingora-proxy/src/proxy_h1.rs
  pingora-proxy/src/proxy_h2.rs
      Adds a `should_retry_response` hook, letting the application decide from
      the upstream's response headers whether a request should be retried.
      Upstream only retries on connection-level failures.

  pingora-core/src/protocols/http/server.rs
  pingora-core/src/protocols/http/v1/server.rs
  pingora-core/src/protocols/http/v2/server.rs
  pingora-core/src/protocols/http/subrequest/server.rs
  pingora-core/src/protocols/http/custom/server.rs
      Adds `Session::enable_retry_buffering_with_limit`, which sets the size
      of the retry buffer per request. Upstream fixes it at 64 KiB, so a
      request body the caller has read in full before proxying is dropped
      from the buffer when larger, and never reaches the upstream. The
      custom-session trait gets a default that falls back to the standard
      buffer. (zentinel-pingora-core 0.9.1)

  pingora-proxy/src/lib.rs
      Adds a test for the per-request retry buffer limit; no functional
      change.

  pingora-core/src/protocols/l4/stream.rs
  pingora-core/src/listeners/mod.rs
      Backport of upstream commit 5b30d71 (after 0.9.0): the L4 buffers are
      held in an enum instead of a zero-capacity `BufStream`, which tokio
      1.54 rejects with a panic on every accept and connect. Adds a listener
      test for unbuffered streams. (zentinel-pingora-core 0.9.2)

No other source file differs from upstream 0.9.0.

The manifests of pingora-prometheus and pingora-foundations differ only in
naming the renamed workspace crate they depend on (`package =
"zentinel-pingora-core"`); their source is unmodified and they are not
republished.

Republished crates
------------------

Five crates are published to crates.io under `zentinel-`-prefixed names, because
`cargo publish` strips git sources and a published crate cannot depend on a fork
by URL:

  zentinel-pingora-core             (modified)
  zentinel-pingora-proxy            (modified)
  zentinel-pingora-cache            (unmodified; depends on the fork's core)
  zentinel-pingora-load-balancing   (unmodified; depends on the fork's core)
  zentinel-pingora                  (unmodified; umbrella over the above)

The remaining crates in this repository are unmodified and are not republished;
consumers resolve them from upstream crates.io.
